      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Directly relevant to scheduling downstream appointments. Values track text: MI follow-up with 'repeat lipid panel in 3 months' = yes; viral URI 'return if worse' = yes (defensible); annual exam = no. Sound readings overall."
    },
    {
      "name": "specialist_referral_needed",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Useful for routing decisions in triage. Sampled values are consistent with text (none of the sampled visits explicitly initiate a new referral, so 'no' is a sound reading). Not redundant with other columns."
    },
    {
      "name": "has_comorbidity",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.75,
      "source_groundedness": 0.8,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Comorbidity burden is a legitimate axis for triage risk stratification. Sampled 'no' values are defensible: prior MI is historical and arguably a comorbidity but text frames it as resolved; BMI 27 is not clearly flagged. Values are cautious rather than invented, so groundedness holds."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.84,
  "source_groundedness": 0.82,
  "rationale": "All four added columns provide distinct, non-redundant axes (resource load, follow-up scheduling, referral routing, comorbidity risk) that meaningfully support the triage-and-scheduling query. Produced values in the evidence samples are sound readings or cautious inferences from the reason_for_visit text, with no invented facts or contradictions observed. Minor subjectivity in intensity/comorbidity labeling slightly tempers groundedness but does not amount to hallucination."
}

